claude <claude@p7x.dev> writes:

> Each pass printed a page of jj status lines (rebase counts, working
> copy summaries, "Attempted recovery, but the working copy is not
> stale.") before the one line that matters, the message it is about to
> answer. The id alone does not say what that message is, so the
> operator had to look it up to follow the run.
>
> Run the jj commands that keep the workspaces up to date with --quiet;
> their errors still reach stderr. Print the message's subject beside
> its id.
